---
description: Never add Cursor Co-authored-by trailers to git commits
alwaysApply: true
---

# No Cursor co-author on commits

- Never add `Co-authored-by: Cursor` or `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` (or any Cursor co-author trailer) to commit messages.
- When creating commits, use only the project's normal author identity; do not append AI/Cursor co-author trailers.
- If a commit message template or tool tries to inject a Cursor co-author line, strip it before committing.
- Do not restore Cursor co-author trailers when amending or rewording commits.
